[ceiling] The lint is wrong for these two faces: each is the roof of a Wago pocket in the east manifold tower, a bridge across the pocket's own span between the tower's two side walls, 8.7 mm over the 221-415 at Z258.15 and 16.1 mm over the 221-420 at Z292.05, with its back edge on the flank. Every line of either roof lands on stock at both ends; the ceiling class reads only a corbel, a column or support as a carrier, not a bridge between two walls.
alternatives: A 45-degree gable over each pocket needs about 4.4 mm (415) or 8 mm (420) more tower above it and bears on the connector's end at two edges only. The side wells' two-tab lid with a 45-degree ramp gives up the flat capture across the connector's end. Support inside a 9.45 mm-deep, 8.7 mm-wide pocket is harder to clear than the bridge it would replace.
